{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. Lottery A is a sure outcome of -500 Euros with 100% probability, so the reference value is -500 Euros. For Lottery A, the only outcome is -500, so the difference from the reference is 0 with 100% probability. For Lottery B, there are two outcomes: -1000 and 0. The differences from the reference value (-500) are: -1000 - (-500) = -500 (with 50% probability) and 0 - (-500) = +500 (with 50% probability). The mean difference for Lottery B is: (0.5 × -500) + (0.5 × 500) = -250 + 250 = 0. The mean difference for Lottery A is 0. Thus, both lotteries have the same mean difference (0), so the decision reason would be indifferent between them.",
